narrative:
The first ships appear as black scratches on the Salt Sea. The harbor office calls them merchants until the third vessel lowers no colors at all. Harbormaster Sten Quill keeps his spyglass trained on them.

@Sten: They do not sail like anyone I know. That is worse than sailing like an enemy.

Coastal Elder Maren Wick is already sending children inland.

Fleet-Marshal Reyva Ashkindle's raiders strike at dawn, disciplined enough to be terrifying. They burn warehouses but leave crates of water at a civilian road. Driftwood Yannic Corr sells a salvaged enemy map for the price of a small house.

@Reyva: I did not choose the war that made my office necessary. I will still finish the duty it gave me.
@Yannic: For half that price, I can tell you which village gets hit next.
